/Title (During the spring of 2026, the CGCS expanded and enhanced its civic learning pipeline through simulations, legal and AI literacy, civic dialogue, partnerships, and student leadership. Looking ahead, the Center will continue advancing a growing range of opportunities that connect students with leadership, public service, applied learning, civic engagement, and community problem-solving. Featured initiatives such as leadership simulations, GAPS, future law programming, student training in conflict management, and the Climate Summit reflect this momentum alongside continued workshops, simulations, collaborations, and additional programming in development.)
